---
Wrapper around `codex` with profile-layered session composition.

Usage: codex-session [OPTIONS]
       codex-session [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  version     Print wrapper and child version details
  completion  Generate a shell-completion script
  config      Operate on config state managed by the wrapper
  profile     Inspect and compose wrapper-owned profiles
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase wrapper log verbosity (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace)

      --log-stderr
          Mirror wrapper logs to stderr in addition to the log file

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-error stderr output. The log file is unaffected

      --silent
          Suppress all stderr output including errors. The log file is unaffected

      --log-format <FMT>
          Format for the stderr log mirror (controls only the mirrored stderr log; the file sink is
          always JSON)

          [possible values: json, pretty]

  -V, --version
          Print wrapper + child version and exit

      --format <FMT>
          Output format for `version`, `config status`, `profile list/show`, and `--version`

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable text output
          - json: Machine-readable JSON output

      --config <PATH>
          Load wrapper config from this explicit path instead of the default user/project locations

      --profile <NAME>
          Select the wrapper profile before any passthrough child argv begins

      --dry-run
          Print the resolved child invocation and exit without running it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Pass-through:
  Any subcommand not recognized by the wrapper is forwarded verbatim to the
  real `codex`. Use `--` to force pass-through of `-`-prefixed arguments.

Environment:
  CODEX_SESSION_CHILD_BIN   Explicit path to the inner `codex` binary.
                            Tried before PATH lookup.
  CODEX_SESSION_LOG_FILE    Explicit log file path. Overrides LOG_DIR.
  CODEX_SESSION_LOG_DIR     Directory holding `codex-session.log`.
                            Rotated daily as `codex-session.log.<YYYY-MM-DD>`.
  CODEX_SESSION_PROFILE     Select the active wrapper profile via environment.
  CODEX_SESSION_REENTRY     Re-entry marker set on the child env to detect
                            chained-wrapper loops. Refuses to start when set
                            to `1` in the parent env.
  RUST_LOG                  Standard `tracing` filter; overrides -v.
  NO_COLOR                  Disable ANSI colors absolutely.
  FORCE_COLOR               Force ANSI colors even when output is piped.
  CLICOLOR=0                Disable ANSI colors on TTY output.
  CLICOLOR_FORCE            Force ANSI colors even when output is piped.

Examples:
  codex-session version --format json
  codex-session config status
  codex-session --profile work profile show
  codex-session --dry-run -- foo bar
